# C++ Standards

| Trigger | Skill |
|---|---|
| Before writing a new class, public API or module | cpp-write |
| Before implementing a plan | cpp-review (plan mode) |
| After substantive C++ changes | cpp-review |
| After L0/L1 MUST findings with a Rewrite Brief | cpp-simplify |

Full reference material: installed cpp/references (here ~/.agents/skills/cpp/references).

## MUST constraints

Prefer established project types; check the reinvention catalogue before utilities.
Follow allocation conventions, RAII and explicit ownership; no raw new/delete.
No namespace/function mutable caches or hidden process-lifetime state. Prefer an
instantiable provider when state is needed. Do not duplicate an existing utility.
Sub0HexGrid scalar kernel is product-neutral, allocation-free and validates failure.

## SHOULD constraints

Use nodiscard on Try/observer/Compute operations and noexcept on pure scalar methods.
Use named predicates, no boolean behavior selectors, pragma once, matching type/file
casing and minimal includes. Raw pointer members require ownership annotations.
Comments explain contracts or rationale; no phase/roadmap narrative in source.
